 \subsection{Integrated GaN Half Bridge}
 \label{sec:hw-halfbridge}
+
+A half bridge contains two electronic switches connected between the positive DC link and its return. Their junction is the switch node. Each switch is a field-effect transistor (FET), whose control terminal is called the gate. The driver converts the microcontroller's low-voltage command into the gate drive needed by the transistor. The MCU pins therefore carry control signals, not the converter's load current.
 
 The LMG2652RFBR was used for the shared switching stage. It integrates two \SI{650}{\volt} GaN FETs, their drivers, high-side level shifting, bootstrap support, current-sense emulation, and protection functions in an \SI{8}{\milli\metre} by \SI{6}{\milli\metre} package \cite{tiLMG2652}. The integrated drive reduces external connections. The board still needs a local bias network, short commutation loops, a controlled switch-node area, and a path for heat removal.
 
